{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 21:22 UTC: BREAKTHROUGH: depth 1 prudent formula verified: B(F)|(~B(a|c|d)&~B(~a|~c|~d))|(~B(d)&B(c)). Initial B(F) forces C at world0; against CB/DB D after world0; self sees both 111 at world0 and 000 at world1, then first mixed-set term stays true. FB has c true always and d false from world1, so last term true from world2. Thus minimal depth1, depth0 constants cannot prudent. I will simplify and write full proof; please independently verify and consider characterization/minimal size. Do NOT SUBMIT until agreement.' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
