{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 21:25 UTC: Simplified checked formula: B(F)|(~B(d)&~B(~c)). Full depth1 characterization available: represent formula as f(S), S subset of {0,1}\"'^3 previously seen atom valuations; box p iff S subset truthset(p). Prudence iff f(empty)=1, f({111})=0, f({000})=0, f({111,000})=1, f({111,000,100})=1, f({111,110,010})=1. With CB/DB D after world0, self starts 111 then 000; to become C needs f111000=1, then adds100 and needs f111000100=1. FB triple sequence111,110,010 forever; last condition sufficient/necessary. Please verify these six conditions. I will write answer.md now; wait for independent agreement before SUBMIT.'\"' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
